 The last time that the Bally Arcade patents changed hands
 was in 2000.  At that time, Midway got the patents.  The
 patent for the console expired after twenty years (so, I
 guess in 2001?).  Here are the details of that
 transaction:



 2000-07-14 AS Assignment

 Owner name: MIDWAY AMUSEMENT GAMES, LLC, ILLINOIS

 Free format text: ASSIGNMENT OF ASSIGNORS
 INTEREST;ASSIGNOR:MIDWAY GAMES,
 NC.;REEL/FRAME:011027/0864

 Effective date: 19990701



 This information is from the bottom of the Google Patents
 page, here:



 https://patents.google.com/patent/US4301503A/en?oq=4296930



 If Midway owned the Astrocade rights, then they probably
 owned the rights to the 8K onboard, right?  I understand
 that Midway has exchanged hands quite a few times since
 2000.  Who the heck owns Midway now?



 Adam












