In a private email to me, "Just
Desserts," who is updating the astrocade MAME driver,
said he has added to the astrocade MAME driver to-do
list:



- Get 300-baud cassette saving working

- Get the Perkins Engineering Blue Ram Keyboard working



He asked me, "If you can supply a list of other things
that need updating and fixing, I'll be glad to take a
look!"



We don't get this opportunity often. What else needs to
be updated? Here is a list of items that I can think off
the top of my head:



1) Astrocade Colors in MAME require fixing - Most of the
colors are close and it doesn't bother me that they
aren't exactly right. However, some of the colors are
completely wrong. What colors are wrong? It would be nice
if there was a comparison showing real hardware against
emulation and a video.



2) Interrupts - I think one of the interrupts in MAME's
emulation isn't supported at all. I can't remember
which one. I presume it is the light pen interrupt. Does
anyone know for sure?



3) What Else? - Where the features are missing from the main
emulation for the astrocade?



I'm sure that there must be other features missing from
the MAME emulation. Can anyone else help me come up with a
short list of the most important features that should be
fixed or added in the MAME astrocade driver?



Adam









